### 5. The Component Unmount Safety Net

If the user abandons the form by clicking a completely different menu item (e.g., navigating away from the Voucher Entry page entirely via your sidebar), React will unmount the component. Add this `useEffect` to guarantee the unlock API fires during unmount.

```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
    // Cleanup function runs when the component is destroyed
    return () => {
      if (lockedVidRef.current) {
        // Fire and forget unlock on unmount
        callApi(`/JS/voucher/unlock/${lockedVidRef.current}`, null, "POST").catch(() => {});
      }
    };
  }, []); // Empty dependency array ensures this only runs on unmount

